  "worked_solution": "First, let's factor out $3$ from the expression:\n\n$$\n12{t}^{2}+75=3\\,(4{t}^{2}+25).\n$$\n\nNow focus on factoring $(4{t}^{2}+25).$  \n\nTo factor a sum of squares, we first write it as a difference. Then, we rewrite the second term using ${i}^{2}=-1.$ Finally, we factor it as a difference of squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{t}^{2}+25 & =4{t}^{2}-(-25) \\\\  & =4{t}^{2}-(25{i}^{2}) \\\\  & =(2t)^{2}-(5i)^{2} \\\\  & =(2t+5i)(2t-5i).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting back, we obtain\n\n$$\n3\\,(4{t}^{2}+25)=3(2t+5i)(2t-5i).\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
